1
00:00:00,850 --> 00:00:06,260
The brush clears a crown. It stands for a city, Kannauj, on the Ganga.

2
00:00:06,260 --> 00:00:13,665
In the eighth century, three kingdoms, one from the north-west, one from the east and one from the Deccan, each wanted it.

3
00:00:13,665 --> 00:00:17,075
Why did three kingdoms fight over one city?

4
00:00:34,950 --> 00:00:40,597
How do we know? Copper plates and temple inscriptions list the kings and their victories.

5
00:00:40,597 --> 00:00:50,097
An Arab merchant, Sulaiman, wrote in 851 CE about the Pratiharas, Palas and Rashtrakutas, and named them as great powers.

6
00:01:06,483 --> 00:01:13,553
After Harsha, Kannauj was the prize of north India. Whoever held it was seen as the ruler of the Ganga plains.

7
00:01:13,553 --> 00:01:21,391
This long contest is called the tripartite struggle, because three powers took part, from about 750 to 1000 CE.

8
00:01:21,391 --> 00:01:27,799
The Gurjara-Pratiharas, from the west, were led by Nagabhata the First and Mihira Bhoja, the greatest of them.

9
00:01:27,799 --> 00:01:37,630
The Palas, in Bengal and Bihar, began when Gopala was chosen king, about 750 CE. Dharmapala and Devapala were great kings.

10
00:01:37,630 --> 00:01:44,792
They supported Nalanda, and founded Vikramashila. The Rashtrakutas, in the Deccan, began with Dantidurga.

11
00:01:44,792 --> 00:01:49,590
Krishna the First built the great Kailasa temple at Ellora, cut from one rock.

12
00:01:49,590 --> 00:01:58,219
Amoghavarsha wrote of poetry and ruled for over sixty years. Each of the three took Kannauj at some point, but none held it long.

13
00:01:58,219 --> 00:02:02,273
The war weakened them all, and opened the way for new powers.

14
00:02:18,650 --> 00:02:26,003
Old name, new name. The old name of the city was Kanyakubja. In time it became Kannauj.

15
00:02:26,003 --> 00:02:30,976
It is still a city in Uttar Pradesh, famous today for its perfumes.

16
00:02:47,350 --> 00:02:58,274
Carve this tip into memory. Pratihara west, Pala east. Rashtrakuta south: Kannauj. Three powers, three directions, one city.

17
00:02:58,274 --> 00:03:00,498
Name them in that order.

18
00:03:16,883 --> 00:03:32,890
Dig Quiz. Pause and name it. Number one. Which city was the prize of the tripartite struggle? The answer: Kannauj. Number two.

19
00:03:32,890 --> 00:03:43,448
Which dynasty founded Vikramashila? The answer: the Palas. Number three.

20
00:03:43,448 --> 00:03:56,321
Which Rashtrakuta king built the Kailasa temple at Ellora? The answer: Krishna the First. Now one line for Mains.

21
00:03:56,321 --> 00:04:01,037
Describe the tripartite struggle for Kannauj and its consequences.

22
00:04:21,417 --> 00:04:30,705
The crown goes into its case. It was the prize for three kingdoms. Three facts to take away. A crown, the prize of Kannauj.

23
00:04:30,705 --> 00:04:41,494
Pratiharas, Palas, Rashtrakutas. The struggle lasted from about 750 CE. Next gallery: The Rajput Kingdoms.

